<title>SWITZERLAND: SNB leaves discount rate unchanged at 1.00 percent.</title>
<headline>SNB leaves discount rate unchanged at 1.00 percent.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank (SNB) said it left interest rates unchanged after the weekly meeting of its three-man policy setting board.</p>
<p>&quot;No change,&quot; a spokesman said.</p>
<p>The rate has been set at 1.00 percent since it was lowered from 1.50 percent on September 26.</p>
<p>At the current level it matches the historic low which was maintained from February 1978 to November 1979. -- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
